=== p2-windows · W7 · page:admin/VehicleCost (WinUI 3 / Fluent) ===
Parity unit : page:admin/VehicleCost   kind=page   web route=/admin/vehicle-cost
Web source  : web/src/features/admin/pages/VehicleCostPage.tsx
ADR refs    : ADR-002, ADR-004, ADR-005, ADR-006, ADR-011, ADR-013, ADR-014, ADR-015
Runner      : .NET 10.0.300 SDK present (dotnet --version 10.0.300) — NOT blocked.

=== APPROACH ===
- The repository's WinUI app is code-first C# (no .xaml page files); every feature surface lives under
  apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/<Name>/ as <Name>.Model.cs (pure, Microsoft.UI-free projection,
  unit-tested headlessly), <Name>.Source.cs (the generated-client feed), <Name>.ViewModel.cs
  (INotifyPropertyChanged + IDisposable state holder) and <Name>.cs (the Fluent view), exactly as the sibling W7
  ApiLogsPage / FeedbackQueuePage / SchemaDriftPage do. The generated prompt's idealized "VehicleCostPage.xaml +
  VehicleCostPageViewModel.cs under TeslaSync/Features/Admin" is mapped onto these real conventions; the surface
  registers itself with the W4 ShellPageFactory by route name ("VehicleCost", already in RouteTable.cs L210 →
  /admin/vehicle-cost) via ShellWindow.xaml.cs.
- Data binding (ADR-004): the manifest data source is useVehicleCost (GET /admin/observability/vehicle-cost
  [limit, since]). The view-model derives the look-back `since` from the selected window (web
  since = now − windowDays·24h) and reads through an injected IVehicleCostFeed; the default EmptyVehicleCostFeed
  resolves the empty state, and the generated-client-backed VehicleCostClientFeed (VehicleCostPage.Source.cs) binds
  to the generated OpenAPI contract client operation get_api_v1_admin_observability_vehicle_cost, passing the
  snake_case `limit`=100 + `since` (RFC-3339/ISO-8601 UTC, matching Date.toISOString()) query params, asserted in
  tests via the FakeApiClient. The route is confirmed in internal/api/router.go ("GET /admin/observability/vehicle-cost")
  and registered in internal/handler/v1/admin_observability_handler.go (h.VehicleCost). No HTTP touches the view. A
  non-success response surfaces as ApiException; the view-model maps StatusCode==503 to the distinct
  subsystem-unavailable banner (web `subsystemMissing`) and every other failure to the generic InfoBar+Retry.
- The response is wrapped by the platform httputil.Respond envelope as {data:{vehicles,totals}} (the web hook unwraps
  via fetchEnvelope); VehicleCostSnapshot.FromJson unwraps the {data:…} envelope before reading the snake_case
  vehicles[]/totals so the wire shape round-trips losslessly.
- The web page renders its states INSIDE the PageContainer body (PageContainer is passed only `query=` for the
  freshness chip, not loading/error/empty), so the native port reproduces them as visible Fluent regions per ADR-006:
  loading -> TsStatGridSkeleton(4)+TsTableSkeleton shimmer; 503 subsystem-missing -> TsAlertBanner(Warning)
  notConfigured; generic error -> TsQueryError (InfoBar-equivalent) + Retry; success/empty content -> the four
  fleet-total TsStatCards + the per-vehicle breakdown TsGlassPanel (window TsSelect + either the shared TsDataTable
  or, when no vehicle ingested, a TsEmptyState). The totals cards + window selector render in BOTH success and empty
  (matching the web, which always renders FleetTotalsCards + the GlassPanel and only swaps the table body for the
  EmptyState). Never a blank region.
- The window selector (web setWindowDays / WINDOW_OPTIONS 1/7/30/90 d, default 30) maps to TsSelect; changing it
  calls VehicleCostPageViewModel.SetWindowAsync(days), which re-projects the selected option + the "Window: Nd"
  sublabel immediately and reloads with the new derived `since`.
- SI units N/A (no unit-bearing physical fields on this admin surface — row counts, byte estimates, rows/min ingest
  rate, DLQ failure counts only); counts format through the shared NumberFormatting port at 0 decimals (web
  fmtNumber) / the rate at 1 decimal (web fmtNumber(v,1)), bytes through FormatBytes (web formatBytes binary
  units + toFixed(1)) and the last-seen stamp through FormatRelative (web formatRelative tiers + absolute MMM d,
  yyyy fallback via DateTimeFormatting), all at the display boundary.
- All 24 manifest i18n keys were added verbatim (web key names) to Strings/en/Resources.resw as
  translation.admin.vehicleCost.* (23) + the reused translation.admin.subsystem.unavailableTitle (already present),
  alphabetically placed between admin.systemStatus.* and admin.xray.*; the four window-option labels
  (window1d/7d/30d/90d) were added too so no literal is hardcoded (resolved but not counted in the 33). The surface
  resolves every label through the ILocalizer facade. The ar/he catalogs lag en by design (translations land later);
  the app falls back to the English default via ILocalizer until translated.
- Microsoft.UI-free Model/Source/ViewModel links were added to TeslaSync.App.Tests.csproj (the bare WinUI view is
  excluded — it uses Microsoft.UI). JsonReadHelpers (internal, ApiLogsPage.Model.cs, same namespace) is reused for
  null-tolerant parsing.
- Build-time defects found + fixed in this surface's own new code (no red shipped): (1) the view omitted
  `using TeslaSync.App.Components.DataDisplay;` (TsStatCard) and `using TeslaSync.App.Core.Feedback;` (CalloutVariant),
  a CS0246 that cascaded into a XAML-compiler WMC9999 internal crash with spurious "Unknown type" noise on unrelated
  components — proven environmental-after-my-change via a pristine `git stash` build (0 errors) then reproduced
  deterministically as the real CS0246; (2) the app project enforces CA1859 as an error, so three private helpers
  (BuildWindowOptions / BuildColumns / BuildRows) were given concrete List<T> return types. Both fully repaired; the
  app + solution now build 0 errors.

